; Tutorial_8_Analyze_a_Dataset.inix -- the pandas Getting Started tutorials, done in DbDo (rewritten 23 November 2026 around
; the Titanic passenger list those tutorials use). A CSV file brought in, with numbers kept as numbers; a profile; filters
; by number, by range and by blank; columns chosen and ordered; a number averaged by group and by two columns at once;
; counts; a column calculated from another; a chart; and the data handed on to Excel. Every answer here matches what
; pandas gives for the same question. NO CODE (24 November 2026, from ChatGPT's review, which Jamal's request already
; asked for): the SQL step left, so every task is a command or a dialog, and the walk is shorter. Query is in DbDo.md.
; notes\DbDo_Pandas_Equivalents.md maps every task of the ten pandas tutorials to DbDo.

[about]
Title=8 - Analyze a Dataset
Intro=The passengers of the Titanic, the dataset the pandas tutorials teach with, brought in from a CSV file and asked the same questions: who was older than 35, how many rode in each class, the average age of men and women, the average fare by sex and class, the surname of each passenger, the longest name, and a chart of ages to hand on.
Setup=DbDo is open, and installed in the usual place, with its data folder.
Homework=Bring in a CSV file of your own -- readings from an experiment, a budget, a fitness log -- and ask it the average of one number for each value of another.

[step]

Say=One want: to learn what a dataset says, the way data scientists do with pandas, without writing a program. DbDo comes with the list they learn on: 891 passengers of the Titanic, with their class, name, sex, age, fare and whether they survived.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus D, D for DbDo, opens it or brings it forward.
Key=Alt+Control+D
Hear=DbDo
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus Shift plus I, Import, builds a DbDo database from another file: a spreadsheet, an Access file, or, as here, a CSV file of comma-separated values.
Key=Control+Shift+I
Hear=Import into a new DbDo database
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type where the passenger list is, in DbDo's own folder, and press Enter.
Type=C:\Program Files\DbDo\data\titanic.csv
Key=Enter
Hear=Imported titanic.csv into a new DbDo database
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A column that holds only numbers comes in as numbers, so age compares and sorts as a number, and a blank age stays blank rather than counting as zero. Alt plus Delete, Say Position.
Key=Alt+Delete
Hear=Position, 1 of 891, 0 percent through
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Before any question, a profile: what each column holds. Alt plus Shift plus S, Generate Statistics. Its kind starts on Profile.
Key=Alt+Shift+S
Hear=Generate Statistics
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus Enter. One line a column: its kind, how full it is, and what matters most. Age is filled for 714 of the 891, from 0.42 to 80, middle 28; survived is yes or no, 342 yes.
Key=Control+Enter
Hear=Profile of 891 records
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape. Now the passengers older than 35. Control plus F, Filter Records, and M for Main columns, a box for each column of the passengers.
Key=Escape
Note=Escape closes the report; nothing new is said until the next key.

[step]

Say=Control plus F, then M.
Key=Control+F
Hear=Filter Records dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=M opens the boxes.
Key=M
Hear=edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus A goes to the age box. I type greater than 35, and press Enter.
Key=Alt+A
Hear=age
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter applies it.
Type=> 35
Key=Enter
Hear=217 records match.
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=217, as pandas finds. Only the names and ages, please: Alt plus S, Show Columns, and T for Type columns.
Key=Alt+S
Hear=Show Columns dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=T for Type columns.
Key=T
Hear=Comma-separated list of column names
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type name, comma, age, and press Enter.
Type=name, age
Key=Enter
Hear=2 columns: name, age
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus O, Order Records, would put them oldest first: age desc. In a box, 2 dot dot 3 is a range; an equals sign alone means blank, and exclamation point equals alone, not blank: 714 ages are known. Control plus Shift plus F, Clear Filter, brings back all 891.
Key=Control+Shift+F
Hear=891
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=And the passengers' columns: Alt plus S, Show Columns, and M for Main columns.
Key=Alt+S
Hear=Show Columns dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=M.
Key=M
Hear=12 columns: passengerid
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Now averages by group. Alt plus Shift plus S, then Alt plus K for the kind, and G for Group.
Key=Alt+Shift+S
Hear=Generate Statistics
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus K.
Key=Alt+K
Hear=Kind
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=G, Group.
Key=G
Hear=Group
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus Enter. It asks which column to group by.
Key=Control+Enter
Hear=Group by which column?
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type s e, for sex, and press Enter. Average which number column?
Type=se
Key=Enter
Hear=Total and average which number column?
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type a g, for age, and Enter.
Type=ag
Key=Enter
Hear=In short, male has the highest average age, 30.7266
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Men averaged 30.7 years and women 27.9. Choosing survived instead of age gives the share who survived: 74 percent of women and 19 percent of men. Escape. Now two columns at once, sex and class: Alt plus Shift plus S, Alt plus K, and C for Cross-tab.
Key=Escape
Note=Escape closes the report; nothing new is said until the next key.

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus S.
Key=Alt+Shift+S
Hear=Generate Statistics
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus K.
Key=Alt+K
Hear=Kind
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=C, Cross-tab.
Key=C
Hear=Cross-tab
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus Enter. The row column: s e, for sex, and Enter.
Key=Control+Enter
Hear=Pick the row column
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter chooses sex. The column column: p c, for pclass.
Type=se
Key=Enter
Hear=Pick the column column
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter chooses pclass. Now a choice: Count records, or Average a number.
Type=pc
Key=Enter
Hear=Count records
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A, Average a number. Which number? f for fare.
Key=A
Hear=Average which number column?
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter.
Type=f
Key=Enter
Hear=In short, the highest average fare is female with 1, 106.1258
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Women in first class paid 106 on average, men in third class 12.66. Then one line for each sex, each class's average, and the average of each class and of all. The same table pandas makes with pivot table. Escape.
Key=Escape
Note=Escape closes the report; nothing new is said until the next key.

[step]

Say=How many rode in each class? Frequency counts the values of the current column. Right Arrow twice goes from passengerid to pclass.
Key=Right Arrow
Hear=survived
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Right Arrow.
Key=Right Arrow
Hear=pclass
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus S; Alt plus C and C for the current column; Alt plus K and F for Frequency; then Control plus Enter. Third class, 491; first, 216; second, 184. Escape.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=A new column from another: each passenger's surname, the part of the name before the comma. Right Arrow once more, to name.
Key=Right Arrow
Hear=name
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Calculate Column has no key, so Alt plus F10, the Alternate Menu, finds it.
Key=Alt+F10
Hear=Alternate Menu
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus F narrows the list.
Key=Control+F
Hear=Filter
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type calculate and press Enter.
Type=calculate
Key=Enter
Hear=Calculate Column
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter runs it. The dialog asks for a name, a kind of formula built on the current column, the formula itself, and which records.
Key=Enter
Hear=Calculate Column dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type surname. Alt plus K, Kind of formula, and T for Text before a comma; the formula box fills with it. Control plus Enter is OK.
Type=surname
Key=Alt+K
Hear=Kind of formula
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=T.
Key=T
Hear=Text before a comma
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus Enter.
Key=Control+Enter
Hear=Column surname added, of text, filled in 891 records, and shown last.
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The formula is tried first, so a mistake changes nothing. Other kinds give a text's length -- the longest name has 82 letters -- a date's year or hour, a ratio, or values mapped, such as male to M. Now a chart for a sighted colleague: Alt plus Shift plus G, Generate Graphics, Alt plus K, and H for Histogram.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus G.
Key=Alt+Shift+G
Hear=Generate Graphics
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus K.
Key=Alt+K
Hear=Kind
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=H, Histogram.
Key=H
Hear=Histogram
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus Enter asks which number column; a g for age, and Enter. DbDo draws the chart and opens a web page: the takeaway, what the chart shows in words, bar by bar, and the numbers as a table, with the picture and an Excel workbook beside it.
Key=Control+Enter
Hear=Histogram
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape. To hand the data itself on, Control plus Shift plus X, Export Data, writes what the grid shows to a file: Excel, CSV, Markdown, a web page and more.
Key=Control+Shift+X
Hear=Export Data
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.


[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I name the command; the reader gives the key.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Bring in a file.
Key=
Hear=Import: Control plus Shift plus I

[step]

Say=Keep only some records.
Key=
Hear=Filter Records: Control plus F

[step]

Say=Choose the columns, and their order.
Key=
Hear=Show Columns: Alt plus S
Hear=Order Records: Alt plus O

[step]

Say=Report on the grid: a profile, groups, a cross-tab, counts.
Key=
Hear=Generate Statistics: Alt plus Shift plus S

[step]

Say=Find a command without a key.
Key=
Hear=Alternate Menu: Alt plus F10

[step]

Say=Make a column from others.
Key=
Hear=Calculate Column: in the Edit menu, without a key

[step]

Say=Chart it for others.
Key=
Hear=Generate Graphics: Alt plus Shift plus G

[step]

Say=Hand it on.
Key=
Hear=Export Data: Control plus Shift plus X
